BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Welcome Day - Fall 2026 Orientation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260908T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260908T160000
UID:welcome-day-fall-2026-orientation@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:Welcome Day - Fall 2026 Orientation\n\nAll new students are in
 vited to Welcome Day\, where we will kick off the academic year. Meet your
  peers\, meet our staff\, learn about our services and supports\, and conn
 ect with the wider neighbourhood and community. 8:30 to 9:30 a.m. Check in
  at the Welcome Tent to get your Welcome Kit\, team button and wristband f
 or refreshments and join your team 9:30 a.m. to 12:30 p.m. Welcome remarks
 \, meet your peers and join in the fun! Meet your Team Captains\, get your
  team pin\, and meet other students from your program and faculty! Collect
  your free Welcome Kit Welcome Remarks with greetings from Indigenous Elde
 r Liz Osawamick\, President & Vice-Chancellor Ana Serrano\, Vice-Provost\,
  Students & International\, Deanne Fisher and your Student Union Check out
  our Student Services Expo where you can meet our staff and learn about ou
 r many supports and resources Participate in creative activities\, insider
  panel discussions\, mindfulness activities\, and chances to win prizes! 1
 2:30 to 4 p.m. OCAD U's annual Community Fair featuring: The Above Ground 
 Art Supplies Art Materials Fair Student clubs and campus organizations\, S
 pecial guest hosts from OCAD U LiVE Enjoy free lunch\, samples\, give-away
 s\, and so much more! 2 to 3 p.m. International Student Coffee Break Level
 s 5 and 6\, 230 Richmond St. West Quiet Space: Need to get away from the n
 oise and action of Welcome Day! for a little break\, meditation\, or quiet
  contemplation? The Student Lounge (MCA 274\, Level 2\, 100 McCaul St.) ha
 s been designated as Quiet Space during orientation. Another option is our
  Multi-faith Room (MCA 657\, Level 6\, 100 McCaul St.). For more informati
 on\, visit ocadu.ca/orientation OCAD U strives to provide inclusive and ac
 cessible opportunities for the entire OCAD U community to participate full
 y. If you require any type of accommodation to participate in this activit
 y\, please let us know: campuslife@ocadu.ca Photography: Please be advised
  that OCAD U hosted events may be documented through photographs and video
 . These images may be used by the University for promotional\, advertising
 \, and educational purposes. By participating in our events\, both on camp
 us and off-site\, you consent to allowing OCAD U to document and use your 
 images and likeness. However\, if you do not want us to use a photo or vid
 eo of you\, please don’t hesitate to let a team member know when you arr
 ive at the event.
LOCATION:Main Building & Rosalie Sharp Centre for Design (MCA) 100 McCaul 
 Street 100 McCaul St.
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/welcome-day-fall-2026-orie
 ntation
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
