BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Creating Participatory Architecture: The Opportunities and Challen
 ges of Inclusive Governance
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260819T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260819T143000
UID:creating-participatory-architecture@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:The Opportunities and Challenges of Inclusive Governance\n\nTh
 e Partnerships for Financial Inclusion invites you to a webinar with Madel
 ine Toubiana (University of Ottawa) and Natalie Eng (University of Alberta
 ). The speakers will explore the possibilities of Participatory Architectu
 re as a community-led and inclusive governance structure\, discussing the 
 benefits and challenges of this form of governance and the importance of a
 lignment with key organizational objectives. This webinar is part of Finan
 cial Inclusion & Resilience Movement (FIRM)'s governance co-design process
 \, facilitated by the Inclusive Design Research Centre at OCAD University.
  The event is free\, accessible and open to the public. Accessibility need
 s can be indicated in the registration form. Register for the webinar
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/creating-participatory-arc
 hitecture
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
