BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:清澈而真实: Pure and True
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260730T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260807T235959
UID:qingcheerzhenshi-pure-and-true@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:An exhibition by Yifan Wang\n\nIn revisiting the city of my yo
 uth\, Beijing\, in 2024 and 2026\, I have noticed the inconspicuous reappe
 arance of Arabic signs that had at one point\, prominently lined halal but
 cher shops in the Hui neighbourhood\, but subsequently gradually had been 
 erased from public view. As a member of the Hui ethnic minority\, I found 
 that the discrepancies between my childhood memories and current Islamic r
 epresentation unsettled my perceptions\, prompting me to observe and docum
 ent these changes. This exhibition invites viewers to the places where I g
 rew up\, to wander through a morning market\, mosques\, public and private
  spaces\, witnessing what has been lost\, what remains\, and what continue
 s to exist beneath the surface. Closing Reception August 6\, 4 – 6 pm Ga
 llery Hours July 30 – August 7\, 2026 Monday to Thursday 7:30 a.m. to 8 
 p.m. Friday: 7:30 a.m. to 7:30 p.m. Saturday & Sunday: Closed Location Ada
  Slaight Hallway (MCA 228)\, 2 nd floor\, 100 McCaul St\, Toronto\, ON M5T
  2W7
LOCATION:Ada Slaight Student Gallery 100 McCaul St. 2nd floor
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/qingcheerzhenshi-pure-and-
 true
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Erdem Taşdelen: THIRDSPACE Artist Talk
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260729T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260729T190000
UID:erdem-tasdelen-thirdspace-artist-talk@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an artist talk by Erdem Taşdelen\, marking the cu
 lmination of his two-month residency as OCAD U’s THIRDSPACE Summer Artis
 t & Mentor-in-Residence.\n\nRSVP here Working across video\, performance\,
  installation\, and text\, Taşdelen's practice explores narrative as a fl
 uid\, constructed form. During time as the 2026 THIRDSPACE Summer Artist &
  Mentor-in-Residence\, he led a month-long thematic program with emerging 
 artists\, alongside workshops and studio visits. This talk shares insights
  into his interdisciplinary approach\, recent projects\, and the ideas dev
 eloped through collaboration\, experimentation\, and storytelling across m
 edia. About Erdem Taşdelen: Erdem Taşdelen is an artist based in Tkaront
 o/Toronto\, Canada. Through the use of diverse materials and media\, he co
 nstructs semi-fictional narratives that incorporate unique historical figu
 res\, events and texts to implicate contemporary sociopolitical realities.
  At the core of his artistic practice lies an exploration of how narrative
  interacts with its form\, and how different forms “stage” narratives.
  Taşdelen has exhibited at venues including The Power Plant\, Aga Khan Mu
 seum and Mercer Union in Toronto\; Contemporary Art Gallery\, Vancouver\; 
 VOX\, Montréal\; Framer Framed\, Amsterdam\; Museum für Neue Kunst\, Fre
 iburg\; and Pera Museum\, Istanbul. He has been an artist-in-residence at 
 the Delfina Foundation and Studio Voltaire\, London\; Hangar\, Lisbon\; Ru
 pert\, Vilnius\; and KulturKontakt\, Vienna. He was awarded the Joseph S. 
 Stauffer Prize in Visual Arts by the Canada Council in 2016\, the Charles 
 Pachter Prize by Hnatyshyn Foundation in 2014\, long-listed for the Sobey 
 Art Award in 2019\, and selected as a finalist for the Taoyuan Internation
 al Art Award in 2025. About THIRDSPACE: THIRDSPACE: Emerging Artist Summer
  Residency is a month-long residency program at OCAD University that bring
 s together a dynamic group of interdisciplinary emerging artists\, includi
 ng those in the early stages of their careers and those embarking on new d
 irections in their creative practices. Each year\, this emerging artist re
 sidency is led by an established artist appointed as THIRDSPACE Summer Art
 ist & Mentor-in-Residence.\n\nRSVP HERE
LOCATION:115 McCaul 115 McCaul Street 115 McCaul Street\, 2nd floor
URL:https://apply.ocadu.ca/register/?id=fd7d8682-b4fe-4fd4-931a-dfe114718a
 e9
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
